// ── The coin's ticker ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// GEU, "Gloobal Energy Unit". One definition, used by every screen that
// prints it, so the ticker cannot say one thing in one place and something
// else in another.
//
// This now matches what is STORED. It briefly did not: the screens said GEU
// while the server stamped 'GC' onto every coin row, because server.js also
// defined a second, different currency called GEU — a growth-bearing
// prototype with its own balance field and supply document. Two designs were
// wearing one name.
//
// That is resolved. Gloobal Coin IS the Gloobal Energy Unit: pegged, 1 GEU =
// ₹1 in both directions, backed 1:1, no growth. The other prototype is
// disabled behind GEU_GROWTH_PROTOTYPE and its reasoning is kept in
// docs/GEU_GROWTH_DESIGN.md, because growth is deferred rather than
// rejected — and when it arrives it belongs to THIS unit, not to a second
// one alongside it.
// ── CEL: THE NAME PEOPLE SEE, AND GEU: THE CODE THAT IS STORED ───────────
//
// The unit is CEL, the "Circular Energy Loop": money that goes round the
// community, 1 CEL is 1 of your own money. Read as cell (stored energy),
// shell (the first money, cowries) or sell; no "said like" line, so all
// three stay open. Chosen by the founder on 10 Nov 2026; for a day before
// it the name was GLEU, "Gloobal Local Energy Unit", which needed "said
// glue" printed under it. CEL is no ISO 4217 code. (GEU was said
// like "goo", which is not a word anyone wants near their money.)
//
// What is STORED does not change. Every coin row ever written carries the
// currency code "GEU", the server stamps "GEU" on new ones, and the ledger
// accounts are denominated in it. Renaming the stored code would mean
// rewriting history or carrying two codes for one unit; neither is worth
// it. So:
//
//   COIN_CURRENCY  "GEU"   the code: what is stored, sent and compared.
//   COIN_TICKER    "CEL"   the name: what is printed, spoken and read.
//
// currencySuffix (backend/utils/format.js) turns the code into the name, so
// a screen that prints fmtMoney(amount, row.currency) shows CEL without
// knowing the row says GEU. Nothing shown to a person may print
// COIN_CURRENCY; tests/gleu-name.test.mjs checks.
var COIN_CURRENCY = "GEU";
var COIN_TICKER = "CEL";
var COIN_TICKER_LONG = "Circular Energy Loop";
var COIN_TICKER_SAID = "cell";

// The same string, under the name the browser-side ledger accounts are
// denominated in. It was declared in backend/domain/coin/CoinService.js,
// which is deleted with the rest of the coin write path — but the ledger
// accounts that hold the HISTORY of what the coin did are still denominated
// in it, and an account whose currency label disagrees with the lines posted
// to it is the exact defect ReserveAccount.js's own comment describes ("It
// said GC while CoinService posted GEU").
//
// Declared above, beside the shown name, so the two are read together.

// What one GEU is worth, and in what.
//
// One GEU is one unit of the reserve currency — that is the peg, and it is
// the same peg for every account. What differs is what a person pays with:
// an account in India pays ₹1 for 1 GEU, an account in the United States
// pays $1 and receives about 85, because $1 IS about ₹85.
//
// This constant is the DEFAULT only. The server owns the real value
// (CoinReserve.reserveCurrency) and sends it with every coin read; screens
// take that when it is present and fall back to this when the server has not
// answered yet. If the two ever disagree, the server is right — this exists
// so a screen has something to render before the first response lands, not
// as a second opinion.
var COIN_PEG_CURRENCY = "INR";


